---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import {
	LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL,
	LICENSE_PATH,
	SITE_BRAND,
	TERMS_PATH,
} from '../../lib/seo';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Refund Policy"
	description="6-Month, 12-Month, and Lifetime include a 7-day trial with a no-questions-asked refund. 1-Month has a 3-day unused trial. Short passes refund only if unused."
	heading="Refund Policy"
	lede="Refund rules depend on the plan. 6-Month, 12-Month, and Lifetime Access include a 7-day trial with a no-questions-asked refund. Short-term passes and 1-Month Pro refund only if you have not downloaded any images."
>
	<h2>1. Overview</h2>
	<p>Refund eligibility is based on the plan you bought:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>6-Month Pro, 12-Month Pro, and Lifetime Access</strong> — 7-day free trial. No-questions-asked
			refund within 7 days of purchase, even if you downloaded images.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>1-Month Pro</strong> — 3-day trial. Refund only if you have not downloaded any images.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>1-Day Pass and 7-Day Pass</strong> — refund only if unused (no image downloads after
			purchase). No calendar money-back window.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		This policy is in addition to any rights you have under consumer law. Those rights are not
		limited by this page.
	</p>

	<h2>2. 6-Month, 12-Month, and Lifetime Access — 7-day trial</h2>
	<p>
		These Long-Term plans include a 7-day free trial from the time of purchase. During those 7 days
		you may request a full refund for any reason — including if you have already downloaded images.
	</p>
	<p>
		After the 7-day trial ends, we do not refund change of mind, unused time, or a plan that has
		already been used, except where applicable law requires otherwise.
	</p>

	<h2>3. 1-Month Pro — 3-day trial</h2>
	<p>
		1-Month Pro includes a 3-day trial from the time of purchase. During those 3 days you may
		request a full refund only if you have not downloaded any library images after paying.
	</p>
	<p>
		After the 3-day trial ends, or after any image download during the trial, the month plan is not
		refundable.
	</p>

	<h2>4. 1-Day Pass and 7-Day Pass</h2>
	<p>
		These short passes do not include a calendar money-back window. You may request a full refund
		only if you have not downloaded any images after purchase. A single download voids the refund,
		even if the pass has time left.
	</p>
	<p>
		Downloads you made as a free member before that paid purchase do not count against a 1-Day,
		7-Day, or 1-Month refund.
	</p>

	<h2>5. How to request a refund</h2>
	<p>
		Email <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from the address on
		your account. Include:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>The email on the account</li>
		<li>The plan you bought (for example 1-Day Pass, 1-Month Pro, or Lifetime Access)</li>
		<li>The approximate purchase date</li>
		<li>A short note if something went wrong (optional, but it helps us improve)</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		For Long-Term plans, request within 7 days. For 1-Month Pro, request within 3 days and only if
		unused. We aim to confirm eligible requests promptly and to return funds by the original payment
		method.
	</p>

	<h2>6. What happens after a refund</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Pro / pass access on that purchase ends when the refund is issued</li>
		<li>You can still use the site as a free member, including 512 and 1K downloads</li>
		<li>
			Files you already downloaded remain usable under the
			<a href={LICENSE_PATH}>Content License</a>, including the attribution requirement
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>7. When we do not refund</h2>
	<p>Except where applicable law requires otherwise, we do not refund:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>6-Month, 12-Month, or Lifetime Access after the 7-day trial</li>
		<li>1-Month Pro after the 3-day trial, or after any library image download following that purchase</li>
		<li>A 1-Day or 7-Day Pass after any library image download following that purchase</li>
		<li>Change of mind, unused time, or an expired plan once the applicable trial or unused-only rule has ended</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>8. Chargebacks and abuse</h2>
	<p>
		If you believe a charge is wrong, contact us first so we can help. Filing a chargeback without
		contacting us may delay resolution. We may refuse or claw back a goodwill refund, and may
		suspend accounts, where we see repeated refund abuse, payment fraud, or automated download
		abuse. See also the <a href={TERMS_PATH}>Terms of Use</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Refund questions for {SITE_BRAND}:
		<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
